  "details": "- Rebase onto vendor 1:9.0.121-1 (upstream tomcat 9.0.121), which also fixes\n  CVE-2025-66614, CVE-2026-24733, CVE-2026-24734, CVE-2026-24880,\n  CVE-2026-25854, CVE-2026-29129, CVE-2026-29145, CVE-2026-29146,\n  CVE-2026-32990, CVE-2026-34483, CVE-2026-34486, CVE-2026-34487,\n  CVE-2026-34500, CVE-2026-41293, CVE-2026-42498, CVE-2026-43512,\n  CVE-2026-43513, CVE-2026-43515, CVE-2026-59083, CVE-2026-59084 and\n  CVE-2026-66299\n- Drop the TuxCare backports for security constraint selection, Context role\n  mapping, FORM authentication constraint refresh, DIGEST nonce count,\n  RewriteValve [N] processing, HTTP/2 authority validation, HTTP/2 allocation\n  leak and WebSocket session tracking; upstream tomcat 9.0.121 contains these\n  fixes\n- Keep the Unix domain socket hardening of the APR/Native connector\n  (AprEndpoint, upstream 894158fd), which tomcat 9.0.121 applies only to the\n  NIO connector\n- Keep the DataSourceRealm role lookup fix for configurations without a role\n  store (upstream 45a3c1ef), which tomcat 9.0.121 does not contain",
